<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Governorate of New Toledo</h1><p class="st-meta">1534 CE – 1542 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Spanish governorate granted to Diego de Almagro south of Pizarro's lands, whose disputed border over Cusco sparked the civil wars of the conquerors.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1534 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro">Diego de Almagro</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro's</a> partner in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, a governorate of 200 leagues south of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/governorate-of-new-castile">Governorate of New Castile</a>. In 1535 Almagro led a large expedition south into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a>, crossing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andecavi">Andes</a> with Spanish soldiers and thousands of indigenous auxiliaries, but found no rich lands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> was more a claim than an administered territory. Its northern boundary was vague, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro">Almagro</a> insisted that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> lay within it. Returning from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> in 1537, he seized Cusco from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernando-pizarro">Hernando</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-pizarro">Gonzalo Pizarro</a> during the rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manco-inca">Manco Inca</a>. War between the two factions followed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro">Almagro</a> was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-salinas">Battle of Las Salinas</a> in 1538 and executed. His son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro-the-younger">Diego de Almagro the Younger</a>, had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Pizarro</a> murdered in 1541 but was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chupas">Chupas</a> in 1542 and executed. That year the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws</a> merged both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">governorates</a> into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/governorate-of-new-toledo.jpg" alt="Governorate of New Toledo" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Ningyou. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cross_of_Burgundy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1534 CE – 1542 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Diego de Almagro, Diego de Almagro the Younger</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, Quechua</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>, <a href="/countries/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, <a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nueva Toledo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1538&amp;focus=governorate-of-new-toledo" aria-label="Governorate of New Toledo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2811 2858 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Governorate of New Toledo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3131 3114L4910 989M3131 3114L2883 2883"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4910 989h0M2883 2883h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3131 3114h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3131 3114h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1538&amp;focus=governorate-of-new-toledo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
